50: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
51:     """
52:     Recolor the large mask crop column-by-column using the separate three-row palette strip.
53: 
54:     Input structure:
55:     - The background is the most common color.
56:     - One large monochrome foreground object is the mask; its bbox is the output region and may contain background holes.
57:     - The remaining foreground is a 3-row palette rectangle with the same width as the mask bbox: two identical color rows and one uniform row.
58: 
59:     Rule:
60:     - Crop to the mask object's bbox.
61:     - For each output column, color mask pixels with the corresponding color from the repeated palette rows.
62:     - Replace background holes inside the crop with the palette's uniform third-row color.
63: 
64:     Key insight:
65:     The grey object is only a stencil; its columns select colors from the legend, while its holes expose the legend's fill color.
